CLASS:: MP1Encode
SUMMARY:: Encode PCM to fields and bytes
CATEGORIES:: UGens>MPEG Audio
RELATED:: Guides/MPEGAudio, Classes/MP1Pack, Classes/MP1Decode

DESCRIPTION::
Analyze mono or stereo PCM into 32 bands per channel. The native codec clock follows the server rate family.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: ar
Start a streaming encoder. An unspecified bitrate selects the layer default.

ARGUMENT:: in
PCM signal, or a two-element array for stereo.

ARGUMENT:: bitrate
Requested kb/s. A control or audio-rate signal can change it at a frame boundary. The object selects the nearest legal rate.

ARGUMENT:: downsample
Native clock divisor from 1 to 6. A reader samples this at start. Connected field streams preserve the original codec clock.

RETURNS:: An MPEGFrame with editable fields, marker, format, byte lanes and status.

EXAMPLES::
code::
{ var f = MP1Encode.ar(SinOsc.ar(431)*0.08); MP1Decode.ar(f) ! 2 }.play;
::
